## Schema mode fixed columns

`id`, `Location Code`, `Programs (category)`, `Activity (program)`, `Session Title`, `Location Name`, `Status`, `Is Active`, `Featured`, `Amilia Link`, `Notes` + dynamic `{group}|{field}` from `instance_schema`. Legacy header `Campus` accepted as alias.

## Upsert keys

1. Row has `id` → UPDATE by id.
2. No `id` → natural key: `location|category|activity|sessionTitle|startDate|campus`.
3. `current_students` never overwritten on UPDATE.
4. Merge `v2_category.config_base` into `instance_data_ext` before validate.

## Import requirements

- `--type <code>` required (e.g. `camp`, `course`, `workshop`).
- Companion `{csvBasename}-schema.json` beside CSV (from export).
- `--type unified` / `--type all` removed — use separate CSV per type.

## Conventions for code changes

- Extend [`import-instances-common.js`](scripts/lib/import-instances-common.js); keep CLIs thin.
- Match Admin API: [`src/app/api/admin/instance/v2/route.ts`](src/app/api/admin/instance/v2/route.ts).
- Log prefix: `[v2_instance]` for server-side logs.
- Schema columns via `csv-schema-utils.buildSchemaColumns(instance_schema)` — do not hardcode new types.
- Reports under `scripts/output/` (generally not committed).

## Catalog import order

1. **Offerings** — [`offering-csv-import.mdc`](offering-csv-import.mdc)
2. **Instances** — this pipeline (one file per offering type)
